===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who or that which floats in a liquid or gas.
## A small suet dumpling put into soup
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Cynthia Harrod-Eagles|title=The Fallen Kings|text=About an hour later a ration lorry found them, and the men were woken again, this time to a good meal of bully stew and '''floaters''' – suet dumplings – followed by cold rice pudding with jam.}}
## {{lb|en|AU}} A [[pie floater]].
## {{lb|en|police jargon}} A [[corpse]] floating in a body of water.
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|author=E. J. Stauffer|title=The Drowning|text=A dock worker saw him floating against a dock pier and called the police. Condition of the body they thought a '''floater''' that had been hit by a boat and cut by the prop.}}
## {{lb|en|vulgar}} A piece of [[faeces]] that floats.
##: {{ux|en|He left a '''floater''' in the toilet.}}
## {{lb|en|basketball}} Early [[layup]] taken by a player moving towards the [[rim]] where, upon release, the ball [[float]]s in the air over the top of a defender before dropping softly into the [[hoop]].
##* {{quote-book|en|title=Basketball Essentials|author=Tarrence Garrison|year=2014|text= The '''floater''' is a high arcing shot that is commonly used to get the ball over taller defenders in the paint.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1991|author=Michael Tippett|title=Those twentieth century blues: an autobiography|page=143|text=''''Floaters'''' [i.e. unofficially circulated books] <!--bracketed part in original text--> had also come into the prison: you could either find them in the library, or they would be given {{...}}}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2000|author=Julian Broadhead, Laura Kerr|title=Prison Writing: A Collection of Fact, Fiction and Verse|page=9|text=His books were ''''floaters'''', banned by the [[borstal]], but copies were smuggled in and from wing to wing.}}
# A person without a lasting affiliation, role, or position normally expected.
## An [[employee]] of a [[company]] who does not have fixed tasks to do but fills in wherever needed, usually when someone else is away.
## {{lb|en|sports}} A [[player]] not affiliated with a team.
## {{lb|en|politics}} A [[voter]] who shifts from [[party]] to party, especially one whose vote can be [[purchase]]d.
## {{lb|en|politics|US}} A person, such as a [[delegate]] to a [[convention]] or a member of a [[legislature]], who represents an [[irregular]] [[constituency]], such as one formed by a union of the voters of two counties neither of which has a number sufficient to be allowed a (or an extra) representative of its own.
## {{lb|en|US|politics}} One who votes illegally in various polling places or election districts, either under false registration made by himself or under the name of some properly registered person who has not already voted.
## An "extra" male at a dinner party, or a young friend of the hostess, whose assignment is to [[entertain]] the female guests.
## {{lb|en|slang|by extension}} Someone who attaches themselves to a group of people, much to the dismay of that group, and repeatedly shows up to participate in group activities despite attempts to get rid of, or “flush,” said individual.
# {{lb|en|ophthalmology}} A [[thread]]like [[speck]] in the [[visual]] [[field]] that seems to [[move]], possibly caused by [[degeneration]] of the [[vitreous humour]].
#: {{syn|en|musca volitans}}
# {{lb|en|insurance}} A [[policy]] covering [[property]] at more than one location or which may be in transit.
# {{lb|en|finance}} A [[floating rate]] [[bond]].
# {{lb|en|surfing}} A maneuver in which a [[surfer]] [[transition]]s above the unbroken face of the [[wave]] onto the lip, or on top of the breaking section of the wave.
# {{lb|en|two-up}} A coin which does not spin when thrown in the air.
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1998|author=[[Queensland]] government|title=Casino Gaming Amendment Rule (No. 2) 1998|url=http://www.legislation.qld.gov.au/LEGISLTN/SLS/1998/98SL233.pdf|text=In this section "floater" means a spin in which at least 1 of the coins does not turn over in the air at least once.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20040730160912/http://www.legislation.qld.gov.au/LEGISLTN/SLS/1998/98SL233.pdf|archivedate=30 July 2004}}
# {{lb|en|prison slang}} A [[book]] [[circulate]]d between [[prisoner]]s that is not part of the official prison [[library]].
# {{lb|en|India}} A [[waterproof]] [[sandal]].
#* '''2017''', ''Woman's Era'' (Delhi Press) (page 16)
#*: Replace your leather sandals with rubber slippers, sandals or '''floaters'''.
# A {{vern|river mussel}} of genus ''[[Anodonta]]''.
# {{lb|en|slang}} A misstep; a ''[[faux pas]]''.
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:error}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Mating Season|author={{w|P.G. Wodehouse}}| year=1949| text=I must let her know I'm here and put her in touch with the general situation so she will be warned against making any '''floaters'''.}}

